1. Why would round() be unsafe for determining the number of paint cans to purchase?
 So that it can measure precise measurements for paint cans in decimals.
2. What is the difference between the exact-can value and the purchase quantity?
An exact-can can provide the precise decimal value needed, while the purchase quantity needs to be a whole number.
3. For a negative decimal number, how would ceil() behave differently from trunc()?
trunc() will always move infinitely to the left while ceil() would move to the right
